1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,617
He survived an atomic bomb...

2
00:00:02,637 --> 00:00:03,783
and then took a train

3
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:04,200
home.

4
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:07,624
Tsutomu Yamaguchi was an engineer

5
00:00:07,644 --> 00:00:08,908
on a business trip in

6
00:00:08,928 --> 00:00:09,579
Hiroshima.

7
00:00:10,329 --> 00:00:11,877
At 8:15 on the morning

8
00:00:11,897 --> 00:00:13,745
of August 6th, the first

9
00:00:13,765 --> 00:00:15,913
atomic bomb exploded just three

10
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:17,032
kilometers away.

11
00:00:17,782 --> 00:00:20,048
Burned, half deaf, and temporarily

12
00:00:20,068 --> 00:00:21,918
blind... but alive.

13
00:00:22,668 --> 00:00:23,812
So the next day, he

14
00:00:23,832 --> 00:00:25,850
boarded a train... and headed

15
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:26,918
home.

16
00:00:27,668 --> 00:00:30,067
Home was... Nagasaki.

17
00:00:30,816 --> 00:00:32,274
On August 9th, he told

18
00:00:32,294 --> 00:00:34,093
his boss what he'd seen.

19
00:00:34,113 --> 00:00:35,707
His boss said: one bomb

20
00:00:35,727 --> 00:00:38,066
can't destroy a whole city.

21
00:00:38,816 --> 00:00:40,733
Then the sky turned white...

22
00:00:40,753 --> 00:00:41,666
again.

23
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:44,550
Same man. Same distance. And

24
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:46,866
somehow, he survived again.

25
00:00:47,616 --> 00:00:50,711
In 2009, Japan officially recognized

26
00:00:50,731 --> 00:00:52,895
him as a double survivor.

27
00:00:52,915 --> 00:00:54,734
He lived to 93, and

28
00:00:54,754 --> 00:00:56,217
spent his life speaking out

29
00:00:56,237 --> 00:00:56,872
for peace.
